# BrainStrike Desktop provider credentials.
#
# Copy to `.env` (or `.env.local`) in this directory for DEV launches, or to
# `<userData>/.env` for a packaged install. Both are gitignored.
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#   1. a variable already set in the launching process environment
#   2. apps/desktop/.env.local   (dev launches only)
#   3. apps/desktop/.env         (dev launches only)
#   4. <userData>/.env           (every launch)
# Nothing here ever overwrites a variable that is already set.
#
# These files are NOT loaded in test mode (--test-mode, ELECTRON_IS_E2E_TEST=true,
# or NODE_ENV=test) so a developer credential can never leak into an E2E run.
#
# Strict format — the whole file is REJECTED (nothing applied) on any violation:
#   - `KEY=VALUE`, no spaces around `=`, no `export` prefix
#   - `# comment` lines and blank lines are fine; inline comments are NOT
#   - values may be bare, 'single quoted' (literal), or "double quoted"
#     (supports \n, \r, \t, \\, \")
#   - a key may not be defined twice
# A rejected file is logged as a startup error and shown in Settings → API Keys.
#
# An environment key is AUTHORITATIVE: it wins over the encrypted keychain, and
# Settings marks that provider as environment-sourced.

# --- OpenAI (first match wins) ---
# BRAINSTRIKE_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# BS_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# AI_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY_V1=
# OPENAI_API_KEY_V2=

# --- Anthropic ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# AI_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Google (Gemini API key from Google AI Studio; Vertex is unsupported) ---
# GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# AI_GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# --- OpenRouter ---
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# AI_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# --- Tavily (assistant web search + web extract) ---
# BRAINSTRIKE_TAVILY_API_KEY=
# TAVILY_API_KEY=
